  "id": "corridoor-generator",
  "title": "Corridoor Generator",
  "category": "Space",
  "description": "Generate a Corridoor Space INSIDE any selected Space (rectangular, L-shape, T/I-shape, stepped or irregular). Three Shape branches — pick one by keeping it connected (or preview all three and delete the spares after commit): 1) RECTANGULAR — Optimise Rectangle inscribes the largest rectangle, its skeleton main run becomes a straight corridor band. 2) L-SHAPE — Optimise Rectangle inscribes the largest L, its skeleton spine (longest branch through the corner) becomes a bent corridor band. 3) SKELETONED — the space's own straight-skeleton network becomes a full corridor web. WIDTH: set 'Path width' on the branch's Skeleton node (it is the corridor width, in metres — node params drive the COMMIT; wired sliders only drive the preview). Run Flow commits each band as a Space with region 'Corridor' (label 'Skeleton Path' — rename to Corridoor in Space Properties). Note: branches 1–2 also commit their inscribed rectangle/L guide Space (delete it if unwanted), and the L branch produces nothing on spaces without a notch (a plain rectangle has no inscribed L).",
